			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule updates with extension-host codegen and bridge shape generation\n\nSynchronize three Element submodules to their latest downstream versions delivering Phase-3 codegen pipeline completion:\n\n- Cocoon (1db2b302): Add extension-host codegen infrastructure mirroring Wind's ServiceSchema codegen but targeting the extHost decorator family. New Extract/IsExtHostFile.ts filters to `vs/workbench/api/*/extHost*.ts`, IterateExtHostDecorators.ts resolves cross-file interfaces and records paired MainThread counterparts, EmitExtHostSchema.ts emits schema files under `Cocoon/Source/Effect/Generated/<Decorator>/`, and RunExtHostCodegen.ts orchestrates the pipeline. Reuses Wind extractors verbatim - no parser duplication.\n\n- Mountain (3f0b6908): Rename binary and library to verbose production profile name (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain). Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier to match, and add duplicate Binary/node entry to externalBin for production node path. Supports multi-profile build pipeline for development vs production builds.\n\n- Wind (5de2328c): Phase-3 codegen pipeline adds bridge shape generation - EmitBridgeShape.ts generates `Pick<...Upstream, ...>` bridge shape files derived from codegen-emitted upstream schemas, eliminating hand-maintained bridge shapes. WorkbenchBridgeShapeManifest provides curated narrowing of 18 upstream members per service. Also adds WorkbenchProductService (IProductService bridge) and WorkbenchProgressService (IProgressService with location handling). LandWorkbenchLayer and Tags updated. prepublishOnly.sh now runs codegen before production build.",
